      The cost function. Should be Equation (22). However, I found it hard for GAMS to converge using Equation (22) only. Therefore, I added some extra cost functions
      to stablize the GAMS solving process. Equation (22) is essentially cost_throughput. cost_distance, cost_transition, and cost_delay are extra cost functions.
      The weights are selected by trial and error.
       
      I guess g here is not same as in the paper. 1 if passed, 0 if did not pass.
       
      you can add pedestrian delay too if this enough did not work
 118  cost..                                                                           f =e= Wv*[f_throughput + f_dist/100 + f_transit*5 + f_delay/50] + Wb*[5*f_bike_throughput]+ Wp*[5*f_ped_throughput]*1.05;
 119  cost_throughput..                                                                f_throughput =e= sum(vehicle_indi(i,j), sum(k, (1-g(i,j,k))));
 120  cost_distance..                                                                  f_dist =e= -sum(vehicle_indi(i,j), sum(k, (s(i,j,k) - s_init(i,j))*gamma(k))) / sum(i, sum(j, vehicle_indi(i,j)));
 121  cost_transition..                                                                f_transit =e= sum(l, sum(k, p_c(l,k)));
 122  cost_delay..                                                                     f_delay =e= sum(vehicle_indi(i,j),  sum(k, wt_init(i,j)*(1-g(i,j,'7'))*gamma(k))) / (sum(i, sum(j, vehicle_indi(i,j))));
 123  cost_ped_throughput..                                                            f_ped_throughput =e= -sum(k, sum(m, q(m,k)*ped_Demand(m,k)));
 124  cost_bike_throughput..                                                           f_bike_throughput =e= -sum(k, sum(n, x(n,k)*bike_Demand(n,k)));
